Top Kubernetes Interview Questions (With Answers)

🟢 Q1: How do you debug a CrashLoopBackOff in a pod?
 🔹 Check logs: kubectl logs <pod>
 🔹 Describe pod: kubectl describe pod <pod>
 🔹 Check if the app is failing (bad code, wrong env, missing secret)
 🔹 Liveness/readiness probe failures can also trigger restarts

🟢 Q2: How do you do zero-downtime deployments in Kubernetes?
 🔹 Use rolling updates (default in Deployments)
 🔹 Set maxSurge and maxUnavailable
 🔹 Use readiness probes to route traffic only to healthy pods
 🔹 For stateful apps: consider blue/green or canary deployments

🟢 Q3: How do you manage secrets securely in production?
 🔹 Use Secrets objects (base64 encoded)
 🔹 Use external secret managers (like AWS Secrets Manager with CSI Driver)
 🔹 Use RBAC to restrict access
 🔹 Encrypt secrets at rest using KMS with EKS

🟢 Q4: How do you scale an application automatically?
 🔹 Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) – based on CPU/memory
 🔹 Vertical Pod Autoscaler (VPA) – adjusts resource requests
 🔹 Cluster Autoscaler – adjusts worker nodes
 🔹 Add metrics server:
Bash
kubectl top pods

🟢 Q5: How do you monitor and log your cluster?
 🔹 Monitoring: Prometheus + Grafana
 🔹 Logging: Fluentd/Fluent Bit + Elasticsearch + Kibana (EFK stack)
 🔹 Use AWS-native tools like CloudWatch Logs for EKS
